  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will write, solve, and graph linear inequalities in two variables.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Determine which side of the line the solutions to the inequality will fall, given a two-variable inequality and the graph of the related equation.</item>
  <item>Describe the graph that represents the solutions to a linear inequality in two variables.</item>
</list>


<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals: </para>
<list>
  <item>2.11.1: Using Computation and Reasoning</item>
  <item>2.11.2: Finding Solutions to Inequalities on the Coordinate Plane<list>
      <item>2.11.2: Self Check </item>
    </list>
    <list>
      <item>2.11.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>2.11.3: Sketching Solutions to Inequalities<list>
      <item>2.11.3: Self Check </item>
      <item>2.11.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>2.11.4: Shading Boundary Line Regions</item>
</list></section>
